This repository is licensed in parts, because it holds several different kinds of
thing and one licence would be wrong for most of them. Every path is covered by
exactly one of the four headings below; where a directory is split, the split is
stated explicitly.

===============================================================================
1. CODE — the MIT Licence, reproduced at the end of this file.

    Everything under `scripts/`, plus `config.example.env` and
    `requirements.txt`.

===============================================================================
2. TEXT, FIGURES AND DERIVED RESULTS — Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
   International (CC BY 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

    Everything under `paper/`, `predictions/`, `prereg/`, `replication/`,
    `figures/`, `docs/`, `spent/` and `audit/`; all top-level Markdown files; and
    the committed JSON result artifacts EXCEPT `estimates_by_org.json`, which is
    a derived work and is covered by heading 4.

    Under `deposit/`: `MANIFEST-v1.md`, `MANIFEST-v1.json`,
    `DEPOSIT_CHECKLIST.md` and `zenodo.json` only.

    Attribution means citing the work as set out in `CITATION.cff`.

===============================================================================
3. THE FROZEN JIRA ARCHIVE — a split, and the split is the whole point.

    Applies to `deposit/jira-caches-v1.tar.gz` and to the untracked `.jira_*/`
    directories it was built from.

    * THE COMPILATION IS CC BY 4.0. The selection of issues, the five-directory
      arrangement, the freeze at a stated instant, and the per-file SHA-256
      manifest are this author's work and are licensed CC BY 4.0 on the same
      terms as heading 2.

    * THE UNDERLYING ISSUE CONTENT IS NOT. The API responses inside the archive
      are Apache Software Foundation issue-tracker content from
      https://issues.apache.org/jira, publicly published by the ASF and
      contributed to it by its authors under the ASF's contribution terms. This
      author claims no copyright in it, licenses none, and redistributes it
      unmodified for reproducibility. Anyone reusing the issue content should
      consult the ASF, not this file.

    This is the same position `deposit/zenodo.json` records for the Zenodo
    deposit, stated here so the two agree. Superseded wording is noted at the end
    of this file.

    PERSONAL DATA. Jira author and assignee display names appear in some records.
    They are public on issues.apache.org. `scripts/pseudonymize.py` removes them
    if a pseudonymised copy is wanted.

===============================================================================
4. THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL AND DERIVED WORKS — governed by their own licences.

    * `estimates_by_org.json` is a derived work of THE PUBLIC JIRA DATASET,
      Lloyd Montgomery, Clara Lueders and Walid Maalej, Zenodo 15719919,
      which is licensed CC BY 4.0. CC BY 4.0 permits this derivation and requires
      attribution of those three authors. That attribution is given here, in
      `CITATION.cff`, and in `paper/numbers.md`. Anyone redistributing
      `estimates_by_org.json` or anything derived from it must carry the same
      attribution.

    * `refminer_*.json` is the output of RefactoringMiner,
      https://github.com/tsantalis/RefactoringMiner, MIT Licence,
      Copyright (c) 2019 Nikolaos Tsantalis, run over public Apache
      repositories. The output is data about those repositories; it is not a
      derivative of the tool, and the tool's licence does not reach it. The
      detector version used throughout is 3.1.4.

    * `hadoop/`, `corpora/` and the probe clones are NOT COMMITTED. They are
      Apache Software Foundation repositories under the Apache Licence 2.0 and
      must be obtained from their own sources. `paper/traceability_probe.json`
      pins a commit sha per project so any re-clone is exactly diffable.

    * `RefactoringMiner/` and `RefactoringMiner-src/` are NOT COMMITTED
      (see `.gitignore`); they are the upstream tool under its own MIT Licence.

